  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inception Coastal Development Jakarta and North-Java</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jakarta Bay and the greater coastal zone of North Java are known to a complex interplay of coastal dynamics, challenges with drinking water supply, population pressures, groundwater abstraction, and land subsidence.In the period 2008-2020 Netherlands provided advice to Indonesia on the complex coastal dynamics around Jakarta Bay, ultimately culminating in the Integrated Flood Strategy Plan 2020 (IFSP). Early 2024, preliminary designs from the IFSP received new attention which aims for operationalization both for Jakarta Bay as well as for the greater coastal zone of North Java, also called Pantura. The ambition of this assignment is to revitalize and transfer the historic knowledge gained and integrate this into a concept paper towards the government of Indonesia (GoI), and to gain insights on ambitions and process timeline of GoI and next steps to further determining the position of the government of the Netherlands towards these developments.</narrative>
  </description>
